FNIRSI DLA-16 (experimental)
===========================

This driver supports the 16-channel FNIRSI DLA-16 over libusb. No firmware
upload is required. It does not implement DLA-32 or DLA-16 Plus support.
The USB VID/PID 1a86:5537 belongs to a shared WCH interface and does not
identify the model uniquely. Scanning requires an explicit conn=BUS.ADDRESS;
automatic scans return no devices. Find the address with lsusb -d 1a86:5537
and grant your user access to that USB device using your local policy.
A global udev rule for this shared ID is intentionally not included.
Replace 4.27 in the examples below with the actual bus and device address.

Acquisition
-----------

The default mode is Buffer, at 50 MHz, with all 16 channels enabled.
Stream requires a USB 3 connection. Maximum rates depend on the number
of enabled channels:

  Enabled channels    Buffer       Stream
   1-2                1 GHz        1 GHz
   3-4                1 GHz        500 MHz
   5-8                1 GHz        250 MHz
   9-16               500 MHz      125 MHz

These are configuration limits, not a validation claim for every mode.
Voltage thresholds are 0.6, 1.6 and 2.5 V. Basic single-channel, single-
condition triggers support low, high, rising, falling and either edge.
The exact trigger sample position has not been established. Multistage
triggers and arbitrary pattern output are not supported.

Examples:

  sigrok-cli -d fnirsi-dla16:conn=4.27 -C D0,D1 \
    -c device_mode=Buffer:samplerate=200m --samples 100000 -o capture.sr

  sigrok-cli -d fnirsi-dla16:conn=4.27 -C D0,D1 \
    -c device_mode=Stream:samplerate=1g --samples 100000 -o stream.sr

PWM0 and PWM1 channel groups expose enabled, output_frequency and
output_duty_cycle settings. Outputs remain active until disabled:

  sigrok-cli -d fnirsi-dla16:conn=4.27 --channel-group PWM0 \
    -c output_frequency=1000000:output_duty_cycle=50:enabled=on --set
  sigrok-cli -d fnirsi-dla16:conn=4.27 --channel-group PWM0 -c enabled=off --set

For older PulseView versions that do not handle a mixed logic-analyzer
and signal-generator device, FNIRSI_DLA16_LOGIC_ONLY=1 selects a logic-
only profile. This hides the PWM groups, uses data_source for Buffer/
Stream selection and limits the advertised sample count to 100 million.

Validation and limitations
--------------------------

Linux hardware checks on 2026-09-15 covered 60-second Stream reception
at 2 channels / 1 GHz, 4 / 500 MHz, 8 / 250 MHz and 16 / 125 MHz through
sigrok-cli with null output. A separate raw USB probe saved about 15 GB
per configuration at about 250 MB/s. The raw-probe result does not prove
live .sr compression at those rates. Known PWM signals were connected
only to D0 and D1; other channels were enabled but not individually
verified with independent signals. Byte counts and short waveform
windows do not establish sample-perfect continuity over a whole run.

Buffer captures were checked at 16 channels / 50 MHz and 2 channels /
200 MHz and 1 GHz. Basic trigger checks included positive and negative
controls at 200 MHz. PWM output was observed up to 20 MHz; its duty
cycle and the acquisition timebase were not independently calibrated.
Other operating systems and hardware revisions remain untested.

The protocol reference is the GPL-3.0 PXView DLA-32 overlay:
https://github.com/TechBirdCompany/PXView-DLA32-overlay
Reference revision: b6fc4e7c075b4553248c78ed5b3c55bcee461410.
Command framing and CRC were independently checked against factory
DLA-Logic 1.0.3. The tests cover captured command vectors, the 64-bit
sample count, bit ordering, sparse masks and Buffer/Stream framing.
